                            <comment id="499704" author="JIRAUSER22000" created="Mon, 17 Aug 2026 07:17:16 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20571" title="sanity-compr: Timeout occurred after 118 minutes, last suite running was sanity-compr" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20571"&gt;LU-20571&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20325" title="sanity-compr test_2030:  'Timeout occurred after 177 minutes, last suite running was sanity-compr'" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20325"&gt;LU-20325&lt;/a&gt; share the same root cause: a deadlock on the shrinker_rwsem lock, because the upstream fix has not been backported to the RHEL 8 (4.18) and RHEL 9 (5.14) kernels.&lt;br/&gt;
The upstream fix is Qi Zheng's patch series converting shrinker_rwsem to shrinker_mutex (main commit 8a0e8bb112af, "mm: shrinker: convert shrinker_rwsem to mutex", first landed in kernel 6.7).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Neither RHEL 8 nor RHEL 9 has backported it. This is confirmed in the centos-stream-8 source (shrinker_rwsem is still there, no shrinker_mutex at all) and on the running kernel (kallsyms on 5.14.0-687 still shows the shrinker_rwsem symbol).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The difference is in how the deadlock is triggered:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20325" title="sanity-compr test_2030:  'Timeout occurred after 177 minutes, last suite running was sanity-compr'" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20325"&gt;LU-20325&lt;/a&gt; (sanity-compr test_2030 timeout) hits it via unregister_shrinker, i.e. the shrinker teardown path, for&lt;br/&gt;
example during filesystem unmount or module teardown.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20571" title="sanity-compr: Timeout occurred after 118 minutes, last suite running was sanity-compr" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20571"&gt;LU-20571&lt;/a&gt; (sanity-compr timeout) hits it via alloc_shrinker, i.e. the shrinker registration path, while the test is generating memory pressure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20325" title="sanity-compr test_2030:  'Timeout occurred after 177 minutes, last suite running was sanity-compr'" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20325"&gt;LU-20325&lt;/a&gt; can be worked around with drop_caches or umount -l style tricks that reduce shrinker activity (mitigation patch 67884 on b_es7_0), which lets the test finish.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20571" title="sanity-compr: Timeout occurred after 118 minutes, last suite running was sanity-compr" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20571"&gt;LU-20571&lt;/a&gt; cannot be worked around this way, because generating memory pressure is exactly the purpose of the test. sanity-compr exercises compression, which deliberately drives memory pressure and shrinker allocation. Any mitigation of that kind would defeat the purpose of the test, so there is no practical test-side workaround.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The only proper fix is to backport the upstream kernel change (Qi Zheng's shrinker_rwsem to shrinker_mutex conversion, commit 8a0e8bb112af and the related series) to the RHEL 8 / RHEL 9 kernels used on the test farm clients.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Besides, maloo shows that RHEL 10 (6.12) clients are not affected, since they have the native mutex (the change landed in 6.7). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also the x86_64 clients are not affected, the bug only happens on aarch64 clients.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
